# What Vercel must not upload.
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS. `vercel --prod` failed with "Request body too large" and the cause
# was never diagnosed, so production was deployed by whatever happened to work. The
# repo carries 1.9 GB of Rust build artifacts in `target/` plus half a gigabyte each of
# `node_modules` and `.next`. None of it is input to a Next.js build; all of it was
# being packed into the upload.
#
# The contracts' SOURCE stays: it is what `execution-wiring.test.ts` reads to check the
# app's mirrored constants against the factory's, so excluding it would break the build.
target/
node_modules/
.next/
scripts/node_modules/

# Never, under any circumstances. These hold a seed phrase.
.env.local
.env*.local
*.wasm
